WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.550
A kangaroo rat lives in the desert.

2
00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:05.240
It can go its whole life without drinking.

3
00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:09.440
Its urine can be about 4 times
as concentrated as a human's.

4
00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:11.470
Your kidneys can shift too.

5
00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:14.010
After heavy sweating, you make less urine,

6
00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:16.060
and it's more concentrated.

7
00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:20.430
So how do a kangaroo rat's
kidneys hold on to so much water?

8
00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:25.660
In this mission, you'll see how a kidney
builds a salty zone deep inside itself.

9
00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:30.070
Then you'll trace the hormone that
sets how much water your kidneys keep.

10
00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:34.690
Your mission: explain how a kangaroo
rat's kidneys hold on to water.
